.TH INVF-VERIFY 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf-verify \- verify an InvariantFS volume's integrity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf-verify
.IR image | device
.RB [ \-\-deep | \-\-verify\-seal ]
.RB [ \-\-ignore\-missing\-codecs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf-verify
checks an InvariantFS volume for structural and content integrity. The
volume is opened read-only and is
.I not
locked: a mounted InvariantFS can be verified while it runs.
.PP
The default pass validates the superblock (magic, checksum, block size),
the block bitmap accounting, and the Meta-v3 base B+ tree. With
.B \-\-deep
every stored byte of every file is additionally decoded through the real
read path - batches, container rebuilds, codec blobs - and checked, so a
deep verify proves the volume serves bit-exact content end to end.
.PP
The
.BR invfs-verify.timer (8)
systemd unit runs a weekly deep verify over the volumes listed in
.IR /etc/invfs/volumes .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-deep
Decode and compare every file's content, not just the structures.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-seal
Read-only seal scrub: report per-group parity drift, change nothing.
Exits 0 clean, 3 on drift, 1 on tool failure. No sweep runs.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-missing\-codecs
Do not fail when a file's codec pack is absent; report those files as
unverifiable instead.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the volume is clean; 1 on any failure (the failures are enumerated
on stderr); 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-fsck (8),
.BR invf-sweep (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
